<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Defend Skill</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Barbarian (guild level 40), Dark Knight (guild level 40)
Practising it needs constitution 50.
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre> defend
</pre>
<p>While known for their headstrong rushes into combat, the Barbarian may also
consider a more restrained approach to combat when the situation calls for it.
By defending, the skilled Barbarian enters a state of preparedness to wait for
an incoming attack. The next blow aimed at them is blocked, and the attacker is
left reeling, slower to strike again. That ends the defence.
</p><p>Taking up a defensive position takes 100 endurance. With less you only exhaust
yourself, losing 40 endurance. Your skill and your constitution decide whether
you manage it; if you fail you fall over, and that too costs 40 endurance. You
can't take up a defensive position while fighting, so do it before the fight
comes to you. The focus required to defend prevents almost all other actions:
you can still look around, see who is about, check yourself (score, status,
inventory, equipment, affect) and taunt, which goes well with it. Enter defend
a second time to stop defending.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
